        "language": "english",
        "review": "If you’ve ever wanted to play a game that feels like it was summoned via an ancient floppy disk ritual at 2 a.m., then Human Sacrifice is absolutely your vibe. \n\nIt’s got demons, moral choices, turn-based combat, and just enough unhinged energy to make you question whether the developer was possessed or just very committed. Is it polished? Not really. Is it subtle? Not even close. But for the price of a gas station energy drink, you get occult chaos, voice acting, and the joy of supporting a project that clearly said “why not?” instead of “should we?” Honestly, skip one coffee and just buy it!\n\n worst case you’re entertained, best case you discover your new favorite weird little cult classic.",
